{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Biological Sequence Clustering.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Biological Sequence Clustering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"biological sequence clustering biological sequence clustering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Biological Sequence Clustering.md","fileName":"Biological Sequence Clustering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Biological Sequence Clustering","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Time-Series and Biological Clustering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Time-Series and Biological Clustering","dataclustering.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Biological Sequence Clustering.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Biological Sequence Clustering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"biological sequence clustering biological sequence clustering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Biological Sequence Clustering.md","fileName":"Biological Sequence Clustering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Biological Sequence Clustering","heading":"Biological Sequence Clustering","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Biological sequence clustering groups DNA, RNA, or protein strings from alignment scores, edit distances, shared motifs, k-mer profiles, or probabilistic models. The appropriate representation depends on whether the target is homology, function, taxonomy, or another relationship.\n\nLarge sequence collections require approximate indexing or representative-based methods because all-pairs alignment is costly. Thresholds translate continuous sequence similarity into groups and can split gradual evolutionary relationships into artificial boundaries.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Time-Series and Biological Clustering","dataclustering.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd